From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:53:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: t8132: keep the J604's own PMGR domain
 policy for now

With the CIO PMGR in the platform data (54485c922f), the T8132 handoff
resolves on the J604 and applies the M4 PMGR policy. The J604 tree here
states its own domains, as the J713's does, and marks atc0_usb_aon and
atc1_usb_aon always-on. The policy gives both domains
apple,inherited-on, and the PMGR driver refuses that pair ("conflicting
inherited power policy"), so neither USB-C AON domain would register.

The rest of the policy changes nothing on this tree. Leave the CIO PMGR
out of the platform data until the board's two domains follow the
inherited-on contract (as on the J713) or the handoff leaves a domain
the board marks always-on alone. The handoff then stops at the CIO PMGR
and applies nothing, as on 7.3.0.aurora1-1.733.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts b/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts
index 13edfc1b94..52d97f73b8 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts
@@ -17,13 +17,6 @@ pmgr: power-management@380700000 {
 			reg = <0x3 0x80700000 0 0x14000>;
 		};
 
-		/* Describes no domain; resolves the CIO PMGR the SoC tree carries. */
-		pmgr_cio: power-management@380780000 {
-			#address-cells = <1>;
-			#size-cells = <1>;
-			reg = <0x3 0x80780000 0 0x4000>;
-		};
-
 		pmgr_mini: power-management@388280000 {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <1>;
-- 
2.43.0

